    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139-a1">

                <pb facs="0122" n="102" xml:id="pg102"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 11, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: You have no doubt been
                    informed that the rebel corsair, the Alabama, arrived to-day at Cherbourg with
                    thirty-seven federal prisoners.</p>
                <p>Like protests as made by me in the cases of the Florida and the Georgia I beg,
                    for still stronger reasons, to extend to the Alabama.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurance of highest consideration with which I have the honor
                    to be, your excellency’s very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Drouyn de l’Huys,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs, Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
